IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cccfa-types`
IMPORT `cccfa-dates`
IMPORT `cccfa-cancellation`
IMPORT `cccfa-interest`
IMPORT `cccfa-hardship`
IMPORT `cccfa-damages`
IMPORT `cccfa-goal`

-- Credit Contracts and Consumer Finance Act 2003 — THE ENCODER'S TESTS.
--
-- Expected values are worked by hand from the Act's text (including its own
-- s 45E example) and the calendar (Labour Day 26 October 2026; 1 January 2027
-- a Friday, so 4 January 2027 is not a working day).

§ `Tests`

mat MEANS LIST Date 10 7 2026, Date 25 6 2027

§§ `Cancellation and disclosure periods (ss 18, 27, 29)`

GIVEN disclosed IS A MAYBE DATE, notice IS A DATE, sale IS A BOOLEAN, paid IS A MAYBE DATE, returned IS A MAYBE DATE, short IS A BOOLEAN, layby IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A Cancellation
cancel disclosed notice sale paid returned short layby MEANS Cancellation OF disclosed, notice, sale, paid, returned, short, layby, mat

disc MEANS JUST (Date 16 10 2026)

#ASSERT `the last day to cancel` (cancel disc (Date 23 10 2026) FALSE NOTHING NOTHING FALSE FALSE) EQUALS JUST (Date 23 10 2026)
#ASSERT `the cancellation is effective` (cancel disc (Date 23 10 2026) FALSE NOTHING (JUST (Date 23 10 2026)) FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `the cancellation is effective` (cancel disc (Date 26 10 2026) FALSE NOTHING (JUST (Date 23 10 2026)) FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `the cancellation is effective` (cancel disc (Date 22 10 2026) FALSE NOTHING (JUST (Date 26 10 2026)) FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `the cancellation is effective` (cancel disc (Date 22 10 2026) FALSE NOTHING NOTHING FALSE FALSE)
-- Credit sale: notice 22 October, cash price within 15 working days: 13
-- November.
#ASSERT `the cancellation is effective` (cancel disc (Date 22 10 2026) TRUE (JUST (Date 13 11 2026)) NOTHING FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `the cancellation is effective` (cancel disc (Date 22 10 2026) TRUE (JUST (Date 16 11 2026)) NOTHING FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `the cancellation is effective` (cancel NOTHING (Date 1 6 2027) FALSE NOTHING (JUST (Date 1 6 2027)) FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `the cancellation is effective` (cancel disc (Date 20 10 2026) FALSE NOTHING (JUST (Date 20 10 2026)) TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `the cancellation is effective` (cancel disc (Date 20 10 2026) FALSE NOTHING (JUST (Date 20 10 2026)) FALSE TRUE)
-- 45 working days from Monday 2 November 2026, over the Christmas break: 12
-- January 2027.
#ASSERT `the latest end of a continuing disclosure period beginning on` (Date 2 11 2026) `, revolving` TRUE `, Matariki days` mat EQUALS Date 12 1 2027
#ASSERT `the latest end of a continuing disclosure period beginning on` (Date 15 1 2026) `, revolving` FALSE `, Matariki days` mat EQUALS Date 14 7 2026
-- Legislation Act s 56 (added after the independent pass): from 31 August,
-- 6 months end at the close of 28 February.
#ASSERT `the latest end of a continuing disclosure period beginning on` (Date 31 8 2026) `, revolving` FALSE `, Matariki days` mat EQUALS Date 28 2 2027

§§ `Interest (ss 39, 40)`

#ASSERT `the most interest at an annual rate of` 0.1095 `on the daily balances` (LIST 1000, 1000, 1000, 1000, 1000, 1000, 1000, 1000, 1000, 1000) EQUALS 3
#ASSERT `the interest for one of` 12 `periods a year at an annual rate of` 0.12 `on an average balance of` 1000 EQUALS 10
#ASSERT `the interest for one of` 52 `periods a year at an annual rate of` 0.52 `on an average balance of` 100 EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `the amount on which default interest may run` (`Default interest facts` OF 200, 5000, 50, FALSE) EQUALS 250
#ASSERT `the amount on which default interest may run` (`Default interest facts` OF 200, 5000, 50, TRUE) EQUALS 5250

§§ `High-cost credit (ss 45C-45I)`

GIVEN rate IS A NUMBER, balance IS A BOOLEAN, last IS A MAYBE DATE
      entered IS A LIST OF DATE
      defence IS A BOOLEAN, compound IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `High-cost facts`
hc rate balance last entered defence compound MEANS `High-cost facts` OF rate, rate, rate, FALSE, balance, last, entered, defence, compound, 100, 32

today MEANS Date 16 10 2026

#ASSERT NOT `is a high-cost consumer credit contract` (hc 49.99 FALSE NOTHING EMPTY FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `is a high-cost consumer credit contract` (hc 50 FALSE NOTHING EMPTY FALSE FALSE)
-- s 45C's example: 40% a year and 20% default interest make 60% on the
-- amount in default.
#ASSERT `is a high-cost consumer credit contract` (`High-cost facts` OF 40, 40, 60, FALSE, FALSE, NOTHING, EMPTY, FALSE, FALSE, 100, 0)
#ASSERT `is a high-cost consumer credit contract` (`High-cost facts` OF 10, 10, 10, TRUE, FALSE, NOTHING, EMPTY, FALSE, FALSE, 100, 0)
#ASSERT `the high-cost contract may be entered into` (hc 100 FALSE NOTHING EMPTY FALSE FALSE) `on` today
#ASSERT NOT `the high-cost contract may be entered into` (hc 100 TRUE NOTHING EMPTY FALSE FALSE) `on` today
#ASSERT `the high-cost contract may be entered into` (hc 100 TRUE NOTHING EMPTY TRUE FALSE) `on` today
#ASSERT NOT `the high-cost contract may be entered into` (hc 100 FALSE (JUST (Date 1 10 2026)) EMPTY FALSE FALSE) `on` today
#ASSERT `the high-cost contract may be entered into` (hc 100 FALSE (JUST (Date 30 9 2026)) EMPTY FALSE FALSE) `on` today
#ASSERT NOT `the high-cost contract may be entered into` (hc 100 FALSE NOTHING (LIST Date 18 7 2026, Date 1 8 2026) FALSE FALSE) `on` today
#ASSERT `the high-cost contract may be entered into` (hc 100 FALSE NOTHING (LIST Date 17 7 2026, Date 1 8 2026) FALSE FALSE) `on` today
#ASSERT NOT `the high-cost contract may be entered into` (hc 100 FALSE NOTHING EMPTY FALSE TRUE) `on` today
#ASSERT `the high-cost contract may be entered into` (hc 20 TRUE NOTHING EMPTY FALSE TRUE) `on` today
#ASSERT `the further costs of borrowing recoverable under` (hc 100 FALSE NOTHING EMPTY FALSE FALSE) EQUALS 68
#ASSERT `the most charge at 0.8% a day on credit of` 1000 `for` 30 `days of credit` EQUALS 240

§§ `Hardship (ss 55-57A)`

GIVEN made IS A DATE, previous IS A MAYBE DATE, agrees IS A BOOLEAN, warning IS A NUMBER, missed IS A NUMBER, since IS A MAYBE DATE, remedied IS A BOOLEAN, foreseeable IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Hardship application`
hardship made previous agrees warning missed since remedied foreseeable MEANS
    `Hardship application` OF made, previous, agrees, FALSE, warning, missed, since, remedied, foreseeable

-- Changed after the independent pass (fork F6): 4 months after 16 June run
-- from 17 June to 16 October, so a further application is allowed from 17
-- October, not on 16 October.
#ASSERT NOT `the hardship application may be made` (hardship today (JUST (Date 16 6 2026)) FALSE 0 0 NOTHING FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `the hardship application may be made` (hardship (Date 17 10 2026) (JUST (Date 16 6 2026)) FALSE 0 0 NOTHING FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `the hardship application may be made` (hardship (Date 15 10 2026) (JUST (Date 16 6 2026)) FALSE 0 0 NOTHING FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `the hardship application may be made` (hardship (Date 15 10 2026) (JUST (Date 16 6 2026)) TRUE 0 0 NOTHING FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `the hardship application may be made` (hardship today NOTHING FALSE 0 0 (JUST (Date 16 8 2026)) FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `the hardship application may be made` (hardship today NOTHING FALSE 0 0 (JUST (Date 17 8 2026)) FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `the hardship application may be made` (hardship today NOTHING FALSE 0 0 (JUST (Date 16 8 2026)) TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `the hardship application may be made` (hardship today NOTHING FALSE 0 4 NOTHING FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `the hardship application may be made` (hardship today NOTHING FALSE 0 3 NOTHING FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `the hardship application may be made` (hardship today NOTHING FALSE 14 0 NOTHING FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `the hardship application may be made` (hardship today NOTHING FALSE 13 0 NOTHING FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `the hardship application may be made` (hardship today NOTHING FALSE 0 0 NOTHING FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT `the last day to acknowledge a hardship application received on` today `, Matariki days` mat EQUALS Date 23 10 2026
#ASSERT `the last day to request information on a hardship application received on` today `, Matariki days` mat EQUALS Date 2 11 2026
#ASSERT `the last day to decide a hardship application received on` today `, information requested` NOTHING `, supplied` NOTHING `, Matariki days` mat EQUALS Date 16 11 2026
#ASSERT `the last day to decide a hardship application received on` today `, information requested` (JUST (Date 2 11 2026)) `, supplied` (JUST (Date 20 11 2026)) `, Matariki days` mat EQUALS Date 4 12 2026
#ASSERT `the last day to decide a hardship application received on` today `, information requested` (JUST (Date 2 11 2026)) `, supplied` (JUST (Date 3 11 2026)) `, Matariki days` mat EQUALS Date 30 11 2026
-- A request after the 10 working days (2 November) does not extend the time
-- (added after the independent pass).
#ASSERT `the last day to decide a hardship application received on` today `, information requested` (JUST (Date 3 11 2026)) `, supplied` (JUST (Date 20 11 2026)) `, Matariki days` mat EQUALS Date 16 11 2026

§§ `Statutory damages (s 89)`

GIVEN k IS A `Kind of breach`, c IS A `Kind of contract`, amount IS A NUMBER, nolimit IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A Breach
breach k c amount nolimit MEANS Breach OF k, c, amount, nolimit

#ASSERT `the statutory damages for` (breach `any other breach` `another credit contract` 50000 FALSE) EQUALS 2500
#ASSERT `the statutory damages for` (breach `any other breach` `another credit contract` 2000 FALSE) EQUALS 200
#ASSERT `the statutory damages for` (breach `any other breach` `another credit contract` 200000 FALSE) EQUALS 6000
#ASSERT `the statutory damages for` (breach `any other breach` `a revolving credit contract` 0 TRUE) EQUALS 6000
#ASSERT `the statutory damages for` (breach `s 18 continuing disclosure` `another credit contract` 830 FALSE) EQUALS 830
#ASSERT `the statutory damages for` (breach `s 25(1)(a) disclosure of a guarantee` `another credit contract` 2000 FALSE) EQUALS 100
#ASSERT `the statutory damages for the simultaneous breaches` (LIST breach `any other breach` `another credit contract` 50000 FALSE, breach `s 18 continuing disclosure` `another credit contract` 830 FALSE) EQUALS 2500
#ASSERT `the statutory damages for the simultaneous breaches` EMPTY EQUALS 0

§§ `The top-level goal`

#ASSERT `the credit position for` (hc 100 FALSE NOTHING EMPTY FALSE FALSE) `, entered on` today `, cancellation` (cancel disc (Date 20 10 2026) FALSE NOTHING (JUST (Date 20 10 2026)) FALSE FALSE) `, breaches` EMPTY EQUALS `Credit position` OF TRUE, TRUE, JUST 68, TRUE, JUST (Date 23 10 2026), 0
#ASSERT `the credit position for` (hc 20 FALSE NOTHING EMPTY FALSE FALSE) `, entered on` today `, cancellation` (cancel disc (Date 26 10 2026) FALSE NOTHING (JUST (Date 20 10 2026)) FALSE FALSE) `, breaches` (LIST breach `any other breach` `another credit contract` 50000 FALSE) EQUALS `Credit position` OF FALSE, TRUE, NOTHING, FALSE, JUST (Date 23 10 2026), 2500
